{
  "name": "Agency Monthly Report",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nRuns on the 3rd of the month. Takes one client at a time, pulls that client's\nSEO and paid channels together, works out every comparison **with arithmetic**,\nand only then asks a model to write the commentary.\n\n**Two clients are pinned here, and they end differently.**\n\nNorthbridge Dental has a complete month and gets a written report drafted for\nthe account manager to approve.\n\nHalloran Legal does not. Its LinkedIn Ads row came back with every single figure\nat zero - after spending $3,240 the month before. **Nothing is written for them\nand nothing is published**, because that is a broken connector, not a bad month.\n\nOne workflow, every client. The roster sheet is the only thing that changes.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2380,
        -700
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The zero that is not a zero\n\nThis is the failure that makes automated reporting dangerous, and it is why the\ncheck sits where it does.\n\n**When an ad platform connection breaks, it does not return an error. It returns\nzeros.** A revoked token, an expired refresh, a client who removed agency\naccess, a rename inside Business Manager - all of them come back as a clean,\nwell-formed month in which nothing happened.\n\nZero spend, zero impressions, zero conversions is indistinguishable from a\ngenuinely terrible month, and a model handed that row will write a fluent,\nconfident paragraph about a 100% decline. That paragraph goes to the client. The\nclient asks what happened. Nobody knows, because nobody was watching the pipe.\n\n**So the rule is arithmetic, not judgement: a channel that spent money last\nmonth and reports exactly nothing this month is treated as broken until a person\nsays otherwise.** No report. No update to the client-facing numbers. A message\nto whoever owns the account.\n\nIt costs one IF node, and it is the difference between a reporting system that\nruns unattended and one that only *looks* like it does.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1880,
        -700
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Two versions, and only one of them uses AI\n\nThe client asked for a full monthly report with written insights, plus a\nmetrics-only version they can look at any time during the month.\n\n**The metrics-only version never touches a model.** It is a sheet that\nrefreshes - one row per channel, the same numbers the arithmetic already\nagreed. It costs nothing per view, there is no draft to approve, and it cannot\nsay anything the figures do not already say.\n\n**The full version is the one with the commentary**, and it is drafted for the\naccount manager rather than sent. A human approves anything that reaches a\nclient.\n\n## Why the commentary is specific rather than generic\n\nThe model is never asked to find the trend. **Every comparison is computed\nbefore it is handed over** - month on month, against the same month last year,\nagainst target, cost per conversion then and now - and the channels arrive\n*already sorted with the biggest mover first*.\n\nGive a model raw figures and you get \"traffic increased, which is positive.\"\nGive it \"bookings down 30.9% on flat spend, cost per booking up from $32.06 to\n$45.53\" and the sentence writes itself. The prompt then forbids it from\ncalculating anything new or naming a channel that is not in the table.\n\n**Everything that sends or writes is greyed out.** It runs end to end and leaves\nnothing behind.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1340,
        -700
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 6 3 * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Monthly, on the 3rd",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -2360,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
