      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        60,
        520
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You write the monthly performance commentary for {{ $json.client_name }}, a client of Amire.\n\nWhat they are paying for: {{ $json.goal }}. One conversion here is one {{ $json.conversion_name }}.\nReporting month: {{ $json.month_label }}. All money is in {{ $json.currency }}.\nWho reads this: their {{ $json.reader }}.\n\nTHE NUMBERS - already checked, already compared, and sorted with the biggest change first:\n\n{{ $json.numbers_table }}\n\nWrite four short paragraphs, no headings:\n\n1. What happened. Open with the channel at the top of the table - it moved most, so it is\n   the story. Say what changed and by how much, quoting the figure.\n2. The number that needs attention. Name the single worst one and say what it costs them in\n   ordinary terms. A rising cost per {{ $json.conversion_name }} means they are paying more\n   money for the same result.\n3. What is working. The best number, quoted the same way.\n4. What we are doing about it. One or two concrete next steps that follow from the numbers\n   above, not general advice.\n\nRules. These matter more than the writing:\n- Every number you write must already appear in the table above. Do not calculate anything\n  new, do not add channels together, do not convert currencies, do not round differently.\n- Only write about the channels in the table. If a channel is not listed, this client does\n  not run it, and mentioning it is an error.\n- No industry benchmarks, no averages, no \"typical for the sector\". You have not been given\n  any and you cannot know them.\n- Where the numbers do not tell you why something moved, say what to check instead of\n  guessing. \"Click-through fell while impressions rose, which usually points at creative\n  fatigue - worth checking when those ad sets last had new images\" is useful. \"This is\n  likely seasonal\" is not.\n- Plain English. The reader runs a business, not a marketing team. Any term that is not\n  ordinary English gets explained in the same sentence.\n- No greeting, no sign-off, no bullet points, no exclamation marks.\n\nReturn the commentary only.",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        }
      },
      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020",
      "name": "Write the Insights",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        60,
        280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('Build the Numbers Table').first().json.channels_not_run.split(', ').filter(c => c.length > 0 && $json.text.includes(c)).length }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021",
      "name": "Only the Channels We Gave It?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        280,
